  "system": {
    "description": {
      "type": "String",
      "label": "Description",
      "value": "<p>With a rug, rope, broom or carpet, you animate an object capable of taking you to great heights. For the duration of the spell, you gain the @UUID[Compendium.wfrp4e-core.items.Item.EO05HX7jql0g605A]{Flight 60} Creature Trait as you ride across the skies on your newly animated servant. The animated object has Wounds and carrying Encumbrance equal to 10 + Willpower Bonus with a Toughness Bonus equal to your Intelligence Bonus. Once the object&rsquo;s Wounds reach 0, it becomes inanimate again, and if you are flying while this happens you fall. For every +2 SL you may increase the Wounds and carrying Encumbrance of the animated object by +Willpower Bonus.</p>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p><strong>Lore:</strong>&nbsp;Arcane Spells summoned from the Lore of the Desert tend to summon or shift large amounts of dust and sands upon their targets or shroud the caster in whirling sands like a desert storm. Whenever a spell from the Lore of the Desert is cast upon a target, that target has their Movement reduced by -1 and cannot Charge for the duration of the round.</p>"
    },
